# scripture-games

Brain-hosted **single** repo. Hub UI is story × game type, not inner `projects/`.

- Play must work via `file://` after clone, and via GitHub Pages (relative asset paths, `.nojekyll`). No PHP, no local server, no database, no bundler or component-framework rewrite, no `fetch()` of `.json` packs. Pack files stay the content store (locked 2026-11-08). Teachers play published packs. A downloaded folder stays the offline copy. Theme, when Luke asks, is a shared CSS pass (one token set, projector type, same chrome). No design-agent for that pass.
- Story packs are JSON-shaped `.js` files, one per story, loaded on demand with a script tag.
- Shared fact: `{ question, answer, clue, response, hint, category, difficulty }`. Trail shows `question` and `answer`. Jeopardy shows `clue` and `response`.
- Pictionary prompt: `{ draw, ref }`. Engine lives in `games/pictionary/`.
- Scripture Chase verse: `{ ref, section, text, summary, questions }`. Engine lives in `games/scripture-chase/`.
- Matching item: `{ id, section, label, image, refs, verses: [{ ref, text }], prompt, source }`. Engine lives in `games/matching/`. Church Media Library copies are allowed in `stories/images/` if `source` and a nearby `CREDITS.md` point at the original page. Not our art. Do not copy Red Crystal or paid printables. Scripture refs use `games/gospel-link.js` so the class can open Gospel Library. Hub footer: `how-to.html` and `credits.html`.
- Games: Jeopardy, Pictionary, Scripture Chase, Matching, and Trail. v1 packs (Job, David and Goliath, Psalms CFM) and requested CFM weeks (Proverbs Sep 7–13 2026, Jeremiah Oct 26–Nov 1 2026, Ezekiel Nov 2–8 2026) include **both** `clues` and `drawPrompts`, and Trail asks those same facts as questions and shows the answer. Ezekiel Nov 2–8 2026 also has Scripture Chase. Isaiah CFM Sep 14–20 2026 is **chase-only**. Isaiah CFM Sep 21–27 2026 is **matching-only**. Keep `david-and-goliath.html` until Jeopardy is proven in class.
- New games and new CFM packs: **Ideas for Teaching Children** first (scriptures + those headings), plus hopeful verses from the lesson intro when Luke asks. Ezekiel Nov 2–8 2026 does that. Prefer hopeful Christ / refuge / Restoration content. Do not pull adult warning sections (pride, Babylon, turning away) or the home-and-church question block as the main class material unless Luke asks. Scripture Helps are a later candidate pool (extra scriptures those pages cite). Do not start that pass until Luke opens it. Current and future weeks first, then previous weeks. He reviews before publish.
- For now each new week is Jeopardy, Pictionary, and Trail, then Scripture Chase after review, and Matching when the week is picture-shaped or Luke asks. End goal: every week, every game. A week stays off the hub until Luke reviews it. Every played card has a scripture the class can open. Pictionary keeps the draw word covered and opens the scripture after the drawing. Bingo, when built, is one shared card: scripture call, visible labels, then read together. Deferred ideas live in `ISSUES.md` under Later. Do not start those until Luke asks.
- Teacher-host + projector. Do not add buzzers, a public authoring form, or a Come Follow Me calendar unless asked. A private editor on this PC may read and write pack files for Luke's review (agreed 2026-11-08).
- Later hub (not now): categories OT / NT / BoM / D&C / CFM-by-date, not a flat story list.
- Canonical GitHub is `scripturegames/scripture-games`. Do not recreate it under `cyberresearch-us`.
- Contract: `AGENTS.md` and `D:\Dev\knowledge\wiki\scripture-games.md`.
